'''''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]''''' returned for its '''tenth series''' and began with the launch show on 15 September 2012. The live shows began on 5 October.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a403163/strictly-come-dancing-return-date-confirmed-watch-series-10-trailer.html |title='Strictly Come Dancing' return date confirmed: Watch series 10 trailer – Strictly Come Dancing News – Reality TV |work=Digital Spy |date= 31 August 2012|access-date=3 September 2012}}</ref> [[Sir Bruce Forsyth]] and [[Tess Daly]] returned to present the main show on [[BBC One]] and [[Claudia Winkleman]] returned to present the results show with Daly. [[Zoe Ball]] returned to present the spin-off show ''[[Strictly Come Dancing: It Takes Two]]''. Judges [[Len Goodman]], [[Craig Revel Horwood]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] all returned and were joined on the judging panel by [[Strictly Come Dancing (series 7)|series 7]] guest judge [[Darcey Bussell]], who replaced [[Alesha Dixon]].<ref>{{cite web|author=BBC Strictly Nora |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/2012/04/darcy-bussell-joins-strictly.shtml |title=Strictly Come Dancing: Darcey Bussell joins Strictly! |publisher=BBC |date= 25 April 2012|access-date=24 May 2012}}</ref>

On 20 June 2012, it was announced that [[Katya Virshilas]] would not return to the show as a professional.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a388441/strictly-come-dancing-axes-professional-dancer-katya-virshilas.html |title='Strictly Come Dancing' axes professional dancer Katya Virshilas – Strictly Come Dancing News – Reality TV |work=Digital Spy |date= 20 June 2012|access-date=22 June 2012}}</ref> It was later announced that [[Karen Hauer]] of ''Burn the Floor'' fame would replace her.<ref name="KarenHauer">{{cite web|author=BBC Strictly James |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/blogs/strictlycomedancing/2012/06/new-professional-dancer-for-st.shtml |title=Strictly Come Dancing: New professional dancer for Strictly 2012 |publisher=BBC |date=23 June 2012 |access-date=23 June 2012}}</ref>

The show was broadcast from [[Wembley Arena]] on 17 November with all proceeds going to the BBC charity, [[Children in Need]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/showsandtours/shows/shows/strictly_come_dancing_2012 |title=Be in the audience – Strictly Come Dancing |publisher=BBC |year=2012 |access-date=3 September 2012}}</ref> The show on 10 November was hosted by Daly and Winkleman, while Forsyth took a break before the [[Wembley Arena]] show.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s104/strictly-come-dancing/news/a432401/bruce-forsyth-to-take-strictly-come-dancing-break.html |title=Bruce Forsyth to take 'Strictly Come Dancing' break – Strictly Come Dancing News – Reality TV |work=Digital Spy |date=22 October 2012 |access-date=7 November 2012}}</ref>

Series 10 was the last series of the show to be produced at the studios of the BBC Television Centre in West London. In March 2013 the Television Centre site was closed for redevelopment, with the production of future series moved to Elstree Studios.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.tvbeurope.com/production-post/strictly-come-dancing-relocates-to-elstree|title=Strictly Come Dancing relocates to Elstree|date=11 December 2012}}</ref>

[[Artistic gymnastics at the Summer Olympics|Olympic artistic gymnast]] [[Louis Smith (gymnast)|Louis Smith]] and [[Flavia Cacace]] won the series on 22 December, while [[Girls Aloud]] singer [[Kimberley Walsh]] and [[Pasha Kovalev]] and actress [[Denise van Outen]] and [[James Jordan (dancer)|James Jordan]] were the runners-up.

